        "# Random Graphs and Network Processes\n",
        "\n",
        "## Project Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "This project investigates structural and dynamical properties of Erdős–Rényi random graphs \\(G(n,p)\\).\n",
        "\n",
        "The study combines mathematical theory with computational simulation to examine how the edge probability \\(p\\) affects:\n",
        "\n",
        "- degree distributions\n",
        "- connected components\n",
        "- giant-component formation\n",
        "- full connectivity\n",
        "- shortest-path distances\n",
        "- random-walk exploration\n",
        "\n",
        "The simulations are compared with theoretical results from random graph theory.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Research Question\n",
        "\n",
        "How does the edge probability \\(p\\) influence the structure and exploration of an Erdős–Rényi random graph?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Methodology\n",
        "\n",
        "Random graphs are generated using the Erdős–Rényi model \\(G(n,p)\\). The investigation uses computational simulations to examine how changing the edge probability \\(p\\) affects graph structure and random-walk behaviour.\n",
        "\n",
        "Repeated simulations are conducted to estimate graph properties, examine variability and compare observed results with theoretical expectations. Numerical summaries and visualisations are used to interpret the findings."
