        "## Theoretical Degree Distribution\n",
        "\n",
        "In the Erdős–Rényi model \\(G(n,p)\\), each possible edge is included independently with probability \\(p\\).\n",
        "\n",
        "For a fixed vertex, there are \\(n-1\\) possible neighbours. Therefore, the degree of a vertex follows a binomial distribution:\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "D \\sim \\mathrm{Binomial}(n-1,p)\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "The probability that a vertex has degree \\(k\\) is\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "P(D=k)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\binom{n-1}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-1-k}.\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "The expected degree is\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "E[D]=(n-1)p.\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "For this simulation, \\(n=100\\) and \\(p=0.03\\), so the theoretical expected degree is\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "E[D]=99(0.03)=2.97.\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "The simulated degree distribution can now be compared with this theoretical binomial distribution."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8aqbyDfTbBDq"
      }
    },
